      <cm:vname>
        <cm:mimedesc cm:id="i87_yRRxTh6LkelFg" cm:mimetype="text/plain" cm:encoding="utf-8">ps:classalias: Variable Base Class for ClassE</cm:mimedesc>
      </cm:vname>
      <cm:desc>
        <cm:mimedesc cm:id="iJb07SpNgLnlc0go9" cm:mimetype="text/html" cm:encoding="utf-8">The ps:classalias element in family models can be used to model a variable base class 
To have class classE inherit either from classA or classB implement classE like this

classE: classD { ... };

and put a 'ps:classalias' classD into the family model, and create restrictions for its attribute 
'Value' to be either "classA" or "classB" as shown in the System.ccfm.</cm:mimedesc>
      </cm:desc>
    </cm:element>
